Army Hospital (Research & Referral), New Delhi, successfully performed Deep Brain Stimulation (DBS) surgery on a 33-year-old serving soldier suffering from young-onset Parkinson’s disease which severely affected his functional capability.

The advanced neurosurgical procedure offers renewed hope of improved motor control, independence and quality of life. The procedure reflects the expertise, multidisciplinary teamwork and commitment of the Armed Forces Medical Services to providing world-class healthcare to its personnel.

